// bTunGsTeN Workbench 001 — SAW plan. STAGED, NOT RUN (2026-10-06).
//
// Software Analysis Workbench (Galois, the tool NSA's Foundation repo
// builds its assurance methodology around) proves an implementation
// equivalent to a Cryptol specification. The spec half exists
// (../wb001-cryptol/Intent.cry, itself staged-unrun); the implementation
// half for SAW is a RUST twin of wb001-intent.mjs that does not exist
// yet — the JS twin is the executable battery's target, and SAW has no
// JS extraction. Named gaps, in order:
//
//   1. cryptol typecheck + :check/:prove wireInjective (CI container;
//      :check is SAMPLED evidence — constructed related pairs required —
//      and is never recorded as the :prove universal result)
//   2. Rust twin of canonical/decode in this repo, reproducing the
//      pinned shared vectors (wb001-vectors.json) byte-for-byte —
//      positives exact, refusals by code — BEFORE any equivalence claim
//   3. this script's equivalence proof against the twin       (last)
//
// Planned shape once (1)-(2) exist — kept here so the run is a matter of
// filling in the bitcode path, not of redesign:
//
//   cryptol_load ../wb001-cryptol/Intent.cry;
//   let wireSpec = cryptol "wire";
//
//   llvm_load_bitcode "target/…/wb001_intent.bc";
//   let canonicalImpl = llvm_extract "wb001_intent::canonical";
//
//   // equivalence, no symbolic exceptions: for all VALID intents the
//   // Rust meaningful bytes are the Cryptol wire's meaningful prefix
//   // (same envLen, same bytes), pinned first by the shared vectors.
//   theorem rust_matches_spec : llvm_verify canonicalImpl
//     [cryptol wireSpec] [];
//
//   // the adversarial leg, mirrored from the battery: after the
//   // equivalence proof, mutation is provably detected — any envelope
//   // differing from canonical i in any bit fails decode or SigVerify,
//   // which is P3 in the .cry file.
//
// Run environment note: SAW release binaries are Linux x86_64; the CI
// ubuntu runner is the qualified host (tests.yml's container beat when it
// lands). Until then: UNVERIFIED, deliberately.
